WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.137
LEAD is the forward-looking counterpart to LAG.

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:08.767
It retrieves a value from the next ordered row.

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:17.892
This is useful for time until next visit, next purchase, or next event.

00:00:17.892 --> 00:00:22.722
Again, the partition and order define the sequence.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:30.247
LAG and LEAD compare a row with a previous or next row in a defined sequence.

00:00:30.247 --> 00:00:37.022
The sequence must be meaningful—usually time plus a stable tie-breaker.

00:00:37.022 --> 00:00:46.356
This is powerful for readmissions, repeat purchases, machine events, and state transitions.
